{"type":"message","id":"b22c01fc","parentId":"1e1d4f4a","timestamp":"2026-05-11T06:34:06.777Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implemented the recommended behavior in `~/.pi/agent/extensions/trail-link.ts`.\n\nNew behavior:\n\n- **On by default** on `session_start` / `/reload` if the current branch has a Trail.\n- Existing replay comments are ignored; only new live comments are sent to Pi.\n- On `agent_end`, it re-checks the active branch/trail:\n  - same trail → keeps watching\n  - different trail → restarts watcher for new trail\n  - no trail → stops watcher quietly\n- No noisy error on startup/reload when no trail exists.\n\nCommand surface:\n\n```text\n/trail-watch\n```\n\nShows/restarts current watching status. If not watching and not paused, starts it.\n\n```text\n/trail-watch pause\n```\n\nPauses watching for this Pi runtime/session.\n\n```text\n/trail-watch resume\n```\n\nTurns it back on.\n\n```text\n/trail-watch restart\n```\n\nForce reconnect/re-resolve active trail.\n\nAlso fixed an internal race where restarting a watcher could let the old process’s `exit` handler clear the new watcher state.\n\nValidated that the extension loads and registers `/trail-watch`. Reload Pi with:\n\n```text\n/reload\n```\n\nand it should auto-start watching the active Trail.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_061f472de89db580016a017859e8288191a5b703812f784a98\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":623,"output":260,"cacheRead":108544,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":109427,"cost":{"input":0.003115,"output":0.0078000000000000005,"cacheRead":0.054272,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.065187}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778481240915,"responseId":"resp_061f472de89db580016a01785911288191a018bb49d557c6b7"}}
