{"type":"message","id":"c17db9a0","parentId":"461abf00","timestamp":"2026-05-11T06:40:28.802Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Probably not needed.\n\nI included `restart` as a manual escape hatch for weird cases:\n\n- SSE child process is wedged but not exited\n- auth/token changed\n- branch/trail metadata changed but Pi hasn’t hit an `agent_end` yet\n- `entire trail watch` behavior changed after reinstall\n\nBut for the intended UX, it’s clutter. Since it’s **default-on** and auto-reconciles on `session_start`/`reload`/`agent_end`, we can simplify to:\n\n```text\n/trail-watch          show status / turn on if paused? \n/trail-watch pause    pause\n/trail-watch resume   resume\n```\n\nOr even:\n\n```text\n/trail-watch pause\n/trail-watch resume\n```\n\nAnd `/trail-watch` with no args just reports:\n\n- `watching trail #348`\n- `paused`\n- `no active trail`\n\nI’d remove `restart` unless you specifically want the debug hatch.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_061f472de89db580016a0179d8a12c8191aa46838a405daa8a\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":7338,"output":202,"cacheRead":101376,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":108916,"cost":{"input":0.03669,"output":0.00606,"cacheRead":0.050688,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.093438}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778481622796,"responseId":"resp_061f472de89db580016a0179d768248191b90add4ce0366311"}}
