 specifically:\n\n```text\n/api/v1/trails/.../code-review/stream\n```\n\nand semantically it’s “live code-review discussion feedback.”\n\nI’d rename the CLI surface to something review-specific.\n\nBest options:\n\n1. **`entire trail review watch [number]`** — nicest UX.\n2. **`entire trail code-review watch [number]`** — most precise, a bit clunky.\n3. **`entire trail review-comments watch [number]`** — precise but too verbose.\n\nI’d pick:\n\n```bash\nentire trail review watch\n```\n\nHelp text:\n\n```text\nWatch code-review comments for a Trail\n```\n\nThen later we can still have:\n\n```bash\nentire trail watch\n```\n\nmean “watch all Trail activity” if/when that exists.\n\nFor the Pi integration, the extension can still call:\n\n```bash\nentire trail review watch --json\n```\n\nor whatever the final shape is.\n\nOne wrinkle: this repo already has top-level `entire review`, but I think `entire trail review watch` is still clear because it’s scoped under `trail`. If we want to avoid overload completely, use `code-review`:\n\n```bash\nentire trail code-review watch\n```\n\nBut I’d still lean **`trail review watch`** for ergonomics.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_061f472de89db580016a017ad9e2f081918b664c8c886f9dee\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":355,"output":844,"cacheRead":110080,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":111279,"cost":{"input":0.001775,"output":0.025320000000000002,"cacheRead":0.05504,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.082135}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778481862793,"responseId":"resp_061f472de89db580016a017ac6e92c819183b25671d3f0fb2d"}}
