{"type":"message","id":"27734769","parentId":"1f21c6c7","timestamp":"2026-05-11T06:46:18.790Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agreed. If this is primarily an implementation/automation primitive, shorter is better.\n\nI’d consider:\n\n```bash\nentire trail reviews\n```\n\nbut that sounds like listing formal reviews/verdicts.\n\nFor “listen for incoming review comments,” I think the best short command is:\n\n```bash\nentire trail listen\n```\n\nWhy:\n- Conveys “subscribe to incoming messages”\n- Doesn’t overpromise “all trail activity” as much as `watch`\n- Natural for SSE/event stream\n- Short enough for scripts/extensions\n- Leaves `trail watch` available later for broad Trail activity\n\nHelp text can clarify:\n\n```text\nListen for code-review comments on a Trail\n```\n\nSo:\n\n```bash\nentire trail listen [number] --json\n```\n\nPi extension would call:\n\n```bash\nentire trail listen <number> --json\n```\n\nAlternatives:\n- `trail follow` — familiar from logs, but still broad-ish.\n- `trail tail` — good for streams, but technical.\n- `trail inbox` — cute, less obvious.\n- `trail observe` — too formal.\n- `trail comments` — sounds like CRUD/list comments, not subscribe.\n\nMy recommendation: **rename `trail watch` → `trail listen`**, with help/descriptions explicitly saying “code-review comments.”","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_061f472de89db580016a017b357e4881918ca33150c77c2327\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":696,"output":274,"cacheRead":110080,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":111050,"cost":{"input":0.0034800000000000005,"output":0.00822,"cacheRead":0.05504,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.06674}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778481971905,"responseId":"resp_061f472de89db580016a017b34092c8191a2eefc00e0f3c6f5"}}
